{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_040 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) at 0.5353 acc. PCA (pca_n2000) clearly outperforms scgpt (~11 pt gap), and concat marginally beats weighted. The largest untested design axis is profile setting: all completed experiments use singleprofile with no aggregation, so we have no evidence on whether multiprofile + aggregation adds value. Question: config_010 extends config_040 by switching to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while holding RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (concat) constant. This isolates the effect of multiprofile + simple aggregation. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly tests the most impactful unexplored dimension (profile/aggregation) on top of our proven best configuration, uses the simplest aggregation (avgpool) to minimize confounding complexity, and avoids simultaneously changing multiple factors. If multiprofile+avgpool helps, it opens a productive exploitation path; if not, we gain confidence that singleprofile is sufficient, saving budget from further multiprofile variants."
}

